  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper proposes QFedFisher, a Fisher‑information‑based aggregation method for quantum federated learning using variational quantum classifiers. On ADNI MRI classification (11 qubits, 60‑layer VQC), QFedFisher achieves 89.9% accuracy vs 88.2% (QFedAdam) and 87.0% (QFedAvg). On MNIST (10 qubits), it reaches 91.2% accuracy compared to 86.3% and 84.8% for the baselines, with ~12–16% additional runtime.",
